From 82f5c53bf79dccc8e5fcc366a846c09beba10e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Golubev-Ciuchea <mgolubev@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Jun 2024 15:54:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vrend_renderer: Emulate OpenGL Transform Feedback advanced
 interleaving features.

Android CTS based GPU tests (dEQP) triggers a fault where virgl tries to
write to multiple buffers using interleaved mode and gl_NextBuffer,
which is not available in OpenGL/ES nor any of its extensions. Note that
tests themselves are not using the gl_NextBuffer.

Emulate support of gl_NextBuffer in virgl by using a combined "shadow"
buffer in interleaved mode only. Data from the "shadow" buffer is then
copied to respective separate buffers (if required by XFB mode) before
memory transfer to guest.

Since host side supports OpenGL/ES only, guest's GFX stack should
announce OpenGL/ES support only as well. In this case, buffer mode set
in in guest via glTransformFeedbackVaryings() can be transfered from
guest to host by extending virgl protocol, and for most of the cases
this mode can be used in XFB directly, without the need to have a
"shadow" buffer. Unfortunately, in some cases, TGSI shader
representation dictates mixed mode usage even if not deemed needed,
hence to use the mode directly it is need to alter TGSI to avoid such
cases.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Golubev-Ciuchea <mgolubev@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/vrend_renderer.c | 202 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 132 insertions(+), 70 deletions(-)

